package CanvasNet {
    part def CanvasNetPptxSystem {
        doc /* CanvasNetPptx is a PowerPoint (.pptx) presentation-rendering system, distributed as the separate DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Pptx NuGet package. This is a multi-phase, in-progress feature. Phase 1a implemented the underlying OOXML (Office Open XML) package layer: opening a .pptx file as a read-only ZipArchive, resolving [Content_Types].xml (default extension mappings and part-specific overrides), and resolving package-level (_rels/.rels) and per-part relationships, including relative-target resolution (for example "../slideLayouts/slideLayout1.xml"). Phase 1b adds the presentation/theme/master/layout/slide model and the placeholder property-inheritance resolver: ppt/presentation.xml's declared slide size and ordered slide list, each slide master's theme (color/font scheme, resolved into DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Canvas.Rgba32 values), structural placeholder-shape parsing for masters/layouts/slides, and the verified ECMA-376 placeholder matching algorithm. Phase 1c adds DrawingML shape geometry and paint resolution: shape transform (position/rotation/flip, group child-coordinate-space composition), preset/custom geometry resolved into the core Geometry.Path type, and fill/stroke resolution into core Canvas paint types plus a stroked outline realized via the core Drawing.PathStroker. Phase 1d (this release) adds DrawingML text body parsing, attribute-level run/paragraph property inheritance (including a slide master's own titleStyle/bodyStyle/otherStyle text-style buckets), word-wrap/alignment/vertical-anchor/autofit text layout, and glyph-ink rendering onto a core Canvas.Surface, resolving typefaces through the core Fonts subsystem and filling glyph outlines via the core Drawing.PathFiller. Pattern/picture fill, radial/path gradients, full group-shape rendering semantics beyond transform composition, bullets/numbering, full text justification, shape-resize autofit, kerning, text clipping on overflow, and a full per-slide rendering entry point are explicitly deferred. No non-placeholder shape enumeration is implemented yet. */

        comment testRef /* Test: test/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Pptx.Tests/PptxSystemIntegrationTests.cs */
        comment designRef /* Design: docs/design/canvas-net-pptx.md */
        comment verificationRef /* Verification: docs/verification/canvas-net-pptx.md */
        comment reqRef /* Requirements: docs/reqstream/canvas-net-pptx.yaml */
        comment /* CanvasNetPptx depends on the sibling CanvasNet system (referenced via a ProjectReference from its own csproj, matching the architecture convention every package-bounded system in this repository follows). As of Phase 1b, CanvasNetPptx uses the Canvas subsystem's Rgba32 type to represent a theme's resolved color scheme. As of Phase 1c, CanvasNetPptx additionally uses the Geometry subsystem (Path/PathBuilder, to build and compose resolved shape geometry) and the Drawing subsystem (PathStroker/StrokeStyle, to realize a resolved stroke's outline). As of Phase 1d (this release), CanvasNetPptx additionally uses the Fonts subsystem (TrueTypeFont/SystemFontCatalog, to resolve a DrawingML typeface name hint and extract glyph outlines) and the Drawing subsystem's PathFiller (to paint resolved glyph ink onto a Canvas.Surface) - each modeled below as a non-owning `dependency` relationship to the existing subsystem part def (not an ordinary `part` usage, which would incorrectly model it as an owned child of CanvasNetPptxSystem), mirroring CanvasNetPdf's and CanvasNetSvg's own precedent of adding a `dependency` edge only at the phase that actually first uses the referenced subsystem (for example CanvasNetPdf's Fonts dependency was added only at its own Phase 4, not at Phase 1). No other CanvasNet subsystem (Codecs) is used yet; a future phase that implements picture fill may add a further dependency edge at that time. */

        part pptxDocument : PptxDocument;

        dependency usesCanvas from CanvasNetPptxSystem to Canvas;
        dependency usesGeometry from CanvasNetPptxSystem to Geometry;
        dependency usesDrawing from CanvasNetPptxSystem to Drawing;
        dependency usesFonts from CanvasNetPptxSystem to Fonts;
    }
}
